1
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,777
Easy with the table. The leg is loose
again.

2
00:00:20,229 --> 00:00:22,369
Is the shim still underneath?

3
00:00:28,457 --> 00:00:31,168
By the broom. I've been looking for it all
morning.

4
00:00:54,514 --> 00:00:58,291
I thought you wanted to take Ma's mug
home.

5
00:01:02,743 --> 00:01:05,345
I'm still using it. There's water in the
kettle.

6
00:01:10,971 --> 00:01:16,352
The buyer says she'll be here at five. Mr.
Nestor will come first.

7
00:01:37,029 --> 00:01:38,108
What for?

8
00:01:45,257 --> 00:01:47,935
I told him he could have the table.

9
00:01:53,486 --> 00:01:55,376
I said we'd talk about it.

10
00:02:19,543 --> 00:02:21,829
I thought we had.

11
00:02:27,771 --> 00:02:30,666
You asked if it would fit in the car.
That's different.

12
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,983
I'll call and ask him to wait.

13
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:16,196
Mr. Nestor, can you give me a minute? I'll
call back.

14
00:03:18,968 --> 00:03:22,743
Yesterday I still had a key. I could come
back.

15
00:03:25,935 --> 00:03:29,989
Today I have to decide what to do with a
cracked saucer.

16
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,637
If you want the table, I'll bring it over.

17
00:03:54,968 --> 00:03:57,652
Where would I put it? My place is crowded
as it is.

18
00:04:01,935 --> 00:04:05,288
Is this where you sat when you had coffee
together?

19
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,090
Ma sat there. I sat here so I could see
her at the sink.

20
00:04:30,968 --> 00:04:33,916
Let Mr. Nestor have it. Tell him about the
shim.

21
00:04:37,935 --> 00:04:41,403
Let's move it aside. It's blocking the
cupboard.

22
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,754
Support the bottom. It got wet once.

23
00:05:06,968 --> 00:05:11,267
Nena. Her handwriting. She still had this
when we moved here?

24
00:05:13,935 --> 00:05:16,118
Yes. I carried it onto the jeep.

25
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,733
This towel was Auntie's.

26
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,444
Ben, stay here. Keep your feet up.

27
00:06:20,419 --> 00:06:22,333
Wait. I can see Ma.

28
00:06:28,839 --> 00:06:32,284
Hold on to me. The floor is slippery.

29
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:56,591
Ma! I'm here!

30
00:07:03,919 --> 00:07:07,912
Cover your nose and mouth. Here, take my
towel.

31
00:07:12,339 --> 00:07:15,388
Why are we moving? She hasn't got in yet.

32
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:42,337
Don't lean out. Sit here.

33
00:07:47,419 --> 00:07:49,526
You still remember her towel?

34
00:07:55,839 --> 00:07:59,743
She pulled me in. I had no slippers.

35
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:25,582
Ma looked at the jeep. I waved.

36
00:08:30,919 --> 00:08:35,102
Someone lifted a sack. When it came down,
she was heading home.

37
00:08:39,339 --> 00:08:41,412
You saw her look at you?

38
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,049
I thought she saw me.

39
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,596
Auntie's name is on the envelope.

40
00:09:54,364 --> 00:09:56,109
Was she going to send it?

41
00:10:06,727 --> 00:10:08,700
I don't know. Let's open it.

42
00:10:45,879 --> 00:10:48,266
Thank you for getting Ben onto the jeep.

43
00:10:58,242 --> 00:11:01,959
I went back to the house. I thought he was
still inside.

44
00:11:10,606 --> 00:11:12,765
I thought he was still inside.

45
00:11:49,758 --> 00:11:51,638
There's more. Here, at the bottom.

46
00:12:02,121 --> 00:12:05,368
I called out to her. I thought she heard
me.

47
00:12:14,485 --> 00:12:17,095
Why did she think I was inside?

48
00:12:53,636 --> 00:12:55,726
She asked me where you were.

49
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:07,368
What did you say?

50
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,829
Lita, where's your brother?

51
00:13:53,657 --> 00:13:56,985
I sent him for his slippers. He might
still be inside.

52
00:14:05,314 --> 00:14:07,921
Get in. Sit next to Auntie.

53
00:14:42,229 --> 00:14:43,670
Ma, I'll wait for you.

54
00:14:53,886 --> 00:14:55,849
Get in, sweetheart. I'll follow.

55
00:15:05,543 --> 00:15:07,514
Lita, give me your hand.

56
00:15:42,457 --> 00:15:44,758
When I looked, you were gone.

57
00:15:54,114 --> 00:15:59,364
I was already on the jeep. Behind the
sack.

58
00:16:05,771 --> 00:16:08,012
I saw you once we started moving.

59
00:16:42,686 --> 00:16:45,061
Why didn't you tell me?

60
00:16:54,343 --> 00:16:58,394
I thought you remembered waking up next to
her.

61
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,978
I remember that. I remember both.

62
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,963
Ben? Can you hear me?

63
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,999
I called for him in the kitchen. In the
bedroom. Even under the house.

64
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,283
His slippers were by the door.

65
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:32,881
I put them in my pocket. He might want
them when I found him.

66
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:39,911
Nena. Here he is. He finally fell asleep.

67
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:47,882
Is he hurt?

68
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:16,876
No. He was just looking for you.

69
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:24,698
Ma?

70
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:34,206
I'm here, sweetheart.

71
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:02,923
The towel is cold.

72
00:20:10,500 --> 00:20:12,187
Hold my hand.

73
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:22,305
Her hand was warm. That's what I remember.

74
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,982
The whole ride, I kept waiting for her to
turn around.

75
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:01,901
We got there together. You didn't speak to
me until that night.

76
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,370
I didn't know how to ask.

77
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:44,977
How many times did you think it was your
fault?

78
00:21:50,419 --> 00:21:53,437
When it rains hard, I still think about
it.

79
00:21:58,839 --> 00:22:02,028
I said you might still be inside. Might.
That's all I said.

80
00:22:25,500 --> 00:22:27,512
That's all you knew then.

81
00:22:33,919 --> 00:22:35,387
Want some coffee?

82
00:22:42,339 --> 00:22:45,436
Yeah. Is there any sugar left?

83
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:12,518
In the tin. Ma only put one spoonful in
yours.

84
00:23:17,419 --> 00:23:19,041
You still remember that?

85
00:23:25,839 --> 00:23:31,766
You're the one who forgets. You used to
ask for two.

86
00:23:52,500 --> 00:23:54,227
Here. You get the mug.

87
00:24:00,919 --> 00:24:02,982
So that's where the saucer went.

88
00:24:09,339 --> 00:24:11,312
I needed something to set it on.

89
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:37,000
Still hot.

90
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:14,024
Sorry. I think I'm early.

91
00:25:20,027 --> 00:25:23,057
That's fine. Let me show you the back
door.

92
00:25:28,054 --> 00:25:31,797
Lift it a little, then slide the bolt.

93
00:25:53,473 --> 00:25:55,147
Like this? There. Thank you.

94
00:26:01,500 --> 00:26:03,307
Here are the keys.

95
00:26:09,527 --> 00:26:12,802
The mug's in the box, with the letter.

96
00:26:34,946 --> 00:26:36,942
Keep a hand under the bottom.

97
00:26:42,973 --> 00:26:44,809
I've got it. Ready?

98
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:52,278
Yeah. Together.
